# Trivy findings triaged and accepted for this repository. Each entry states WHY —
# an unexplained ignore is a suppressed defect, not an accepted risk. Keep this list
# consistent with `rust/.cargo/audit.toml` and `rust/deny.toml`, which triage the same
# advisories under their RUSTSEC ids.

# --- rustls-webpki 0.101.7, reached ONLY through the MSSQL client ------------------------
# Chain: tiberius 0.12 -> tokio-rustls 0.24 -> rustls 0.21 -> rustls-webpki 0.101.7.
# UPSTREAM-BLOCKED: tiberius (including its main branch) still pins tokio-rustls 0.24, so no
# version of the MSSQL driver exists that carries a patched webpki. The reachable surface is
# TLS to a CONFIGURED SQL Server — certificate/CRL material arrives over a link the operator
# already trusts, and the impact is a parse panic (DoS), not a bypass. Re-check whenever
# tiberius cuts a release on rustls 0.23+.
# = RUSTSEC-2026-0104 (CRL BIT STRING parse panic)
GHSA-82j2-j2ch-gfr8
# = RUSTSEC-2026-0098 / -0099 (name constraints accepted where they should not be)
GHSA-965h-392x-2mh5
GHSA-xgp8-3hg3-c2mh

# --- astral-tokio-tar, DEV/TEST ONLY ----------------------------------------------------
# Reached only through `testcontainers`, a dev-dependency: it unpacks archives the test
# harness itself produced, on a developer/CI machine, and is absent from every shipped
# artifact (engine binary, container image, CLI). No release path consumes it.
# = RUSTSEC-2026-0145 / -0112 / -0066 / -0113
CVE-2026-32766
GHSA-3cv2-h65g-fgmm
GHSA-fp55-jw48-c537
GHSA-xx64-wwv2-hcqq

# --- DS-0026 "No HEALTHCHECK defined" (rust/Dockerfile) ---------------------------------
# The runtime base is distroless: no shell, no curl, no wget, so a Dockerfile HEALTHCHECK
# would need a health-probing mode inside the engine binary itself. The deployment target
# is Kubernetes, which ignores Docker HEALTHCHECK entirely and uses its own probes — and
# those ARE wired, against endpoints that report real internals: `GET /sutra/health/live`
# (503 + `data.deadLanes` when an execution lane has died) and `GET /sutra/health/ready`.
# See deploy/modules/sutra/main.tf. Adding a HEALTHCHECK here would satisfy the scanner
# without improving any deployment we ship.
DS-0026
